as it relates to energy in Africa?

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:15.245
And also I would love to know a little bit
more about the work that you're doing,

00:23:15.245 --> 00:23:18.014
I believe through Transcorp,
to address this.

00:23:18.014 --> 00:23:25.765
&gt;&gt; So access to electricity
is extremely poor in Africa.

00:23:25.765 --> 00:23:33.931
Less than 35% of our people have access
to reliable electricity on the continent.

00:23:33.931 --> 00:23:37.370
This is a continent of young people.

00:23:37.370 --> 00:23:41.104
Over 700 million people
are young on the continent,

00:23:41.104 --> 00:23:46.200
under the age of 30, and yet access
to electricity is almost impossible.

00:23:48.450 --> 00:23:52.500
These young ones are in
a very competitive world.

00:23:52.500 --> 00:23:56.562
They're going to compete
with children who are used

00:23:56.562 --> 00:24:00.450
to 24/7 uninterrupted electricity supply.

00:24:01.470 --> 00:24:06.608
So the world we see ahead is actually
frightening because the divide

00:24:06.608 --> 00:24:11.475
we want to breach is not the case
happening in the digital space,

00:24:11.475 --> 00:24:14.269
is not happening because of access,

00:24:14.269 --> 00:24:18.980
lack of access to reliable source
of energy on the continent.

00:24:20.580 --> 00:24:25.329
And from the work we do at
the Tony Elumelu Foundation,

00:24:25.329 --> 00:24:31.110
from our close interaction with
young Africans, male, female,

00:24:31.110 --> 00:24:37.010
we know, we can tell, we see,
we hear, listen to them.

00:24:37.010 --> 00:24:42.461
That access to electricity
is a major hindrance,

00:24:42.461 --> 00:24:47.014
constraint on their ability to succeed.

00:24:47.014 --> 00:24:51.936
I'm sure at Stanford,
you might have seen this in your

00:24:51.936 --> 00:24:56.323
business research studies,
that most small and

00:24:56.323 --> 00:25:02.761
medium scale enterprises on
the continent die, they don't succeed.

00:25:02.761 --> 00:25:08.561
And single most important factor for
this due to poor access to electricity.

00:25:08.561 --> 00:25:13.001
So to us as a group,
we believe in the concept and

00:25:13.001 --> 00:25:18.773
philosophy of africapitalism,
which is a call on the private

00:25:18.773 --> 00:25:23.885
sector to play some role in
developing our continent.

00:25:23.885 --> 00:25:27.228
It's a realization that the private
sector has a role to play in

00:25:27.228 --> 00:25:28.750
developing the continent.

00:25:30.250 --> 00:25:35.354
And in practicalizing this,
and not just speaking to it,

00:25:35.354 --> 00:25:39.625
we decided that the power
sector was critical for

00:25:39.625 --> 00:25:45.375
us to invest in as we mobilize
resources and invest in this space.

00:25:45.375 --> 00:25:53.293
Today, we have capacity to generate
about 2000 megawatts of electricity.

00:25:53.293 --> 00:26:01.913
But we have some other hindrances like
gas supply and grid connectivity.

00:26:01.913 --> 00:26:07.660
So we're able to generate about 700
megawatts out of the capacity of 2,000.

00:26:07.660 --> 00:26:15.150
But we're happy that we're
playing a key role in this area.

00:26:16.450 --> 00:26:20.727
But my message always has been to
investors, we've been on this trip,

00:26:20.727 --> 00:26:24.026
